55,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option A sounds great because we wouldn't have to worry about every single switch in the winter.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A provides stability, but Option C is the simplest. However, B is the only one that's truly fair.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option B sounds like a total nightmare to manage. I'm leaning towards C for simplicity.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C is what we have now, essentially. Option B is the only way to stop the subsidizing.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option B creates too much bookkeeping. Option A or C would be much quieter for the house.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, is the unfairness really worse than everyone feeling like they can't use the heat?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Rin, if we go with C, the seasonal spikes will still be a shock to our wallets.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, but A requires a year-end settlement, which I bet is a huge pain to calculate.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, yes, because the usage gap is massive. But I admit the cost of meters is a hurdle.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, if we choose B, we'll just be arguing over the shared area costs instead.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm voting for A. I want us to actually feel comfortable in our own home.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I'll vote for A. It balances the seasonal cost and avoids the high installation fee of B.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Rin,,I can't do B. I'll vote for C because it's the least amount of work for everyone.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I still prefer B for fairness, but if the cost is too high, I'll go with A to at least stabilize the monthly cost.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'll vote for A. It removes the monthly tension of fluctuating bills.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
